Accept faces from an external detector for face-based 3A

The AIQ takes face rectangles for face-weighted exposure, but only
Intel's PVL detector fills them and the Linux release does not ship it;
and isFaceAeEnabled() also requires an advertised face detect mode,
which would add the HAL's own face stream for that missing detector.

Add Parameters::setFaceRegions / getFaceRegions
(CAMERA_STATISTICS_FACE_RECTANGLES, active-array pixels) and
PlatformData::isExternalFaceAeEnabled() (the profile's "faceAeEnabled"
alone). In CameraHal::setParameters, convert the faces to IA
coordinates and store them in AiqResultStorage the way
FaceDetectionPVL does, marked as a CenterNet detector (what the Windows
stack reports for its own); AiqEngine passes them to the AIQ when either
check is true.

Surface Pro 12 (Intel), sp12-camera-hal.

